<title>ITALY: Mondadori shares fall on MD resignation.</title>
<headline>Mondadori shares fall on MD resignation.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Italian publisher Mondadori opened six percent lower on Tuesday after the sudden resignation of Managing Director Paolo Forlin only six months after his appointment.</p>
<p>Mondadori shares opened six percent down from Monday's close at 12,950 lire in thin trading volume.</p>
<p>The company announced Forlin's resignation shortly before trading on the bourse opened and said that a board meeting had been called for February 20 to discuss a successor.</p>
<p>--Milan newsroom +392-66102321</p>
</text>
